<title>USA: IBM CEO's speech over, no profit warning.</title>
<headline>IBM CEO's speech over, no profit warning.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A speech delivered by International Business Machines Corp's chairman and chief executive Louis Gerstner at a trade show on Wednesday concluded without any reference to the company's profit outlook.</p>
<p>Gerstner delivered the keynote address at the Internet World trade show here.</p>
<p>Rumors arose earlier that IBM might be on the verge of issuing a profit warning.  IBM had no comment on the rumors, and said it would issue no press release Wednesday.</p>
<p>Analysts in the U.S. expressed skepticism that such a warning was in the works.</p>
<p>-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730.</p>
</text>
